      "id": "85e18ad1-2d34-48fc-8ee1-e6074070ef81",
      "timestamp": "2026-06-30T14:51:09.370Z",
      "summaries": {
        "brief": "Hardware-level attestation is a state-sanctioned master key that creates a catastrophic single point of failure by baking backdoors into our silicon. History proves that these 'security' features are inevitably weaponized by the very adversaries they claim to deter. A backdoor for the government is a vulnerability for everyone.",
        "medium": "Hardware-level attestation is not a safety mechanism; it is a centralized surveillance architecture that mandates backdoors, creating a brittle bottleneck susceptible to state actors and criminal syndicates. By forcing compliance that only massive, incumbent corporations can afford, this framework effectively destroys open-source competition and consolidates control under a 'tech royalty' model. \n\nWhile proponents argue this mandates security, it ignores the reality of a globalized, fragmented supply chain where full-stack control is structurally infeasible. We are not building a kill-switch for AI; we are building a national vulnerability that ensures when the inevitable breach occurs, the entire infrastructure will be exposed to those we intend to keep out."
      }
