        "brief": "Distributed audits are merely post-mortem logs that cannot stop catastrophic AI-driven pathogen synthesis occurring in seconds. We must replace retrospective monitoring with silicon-level, immutable circuit breakers to ensure human control. Auditing the corpse of civilization is no substitute for preventing its murder.",
        "medium": "While distributed cryptographic auditing provides a record of activity, it is fundamentally incapable of preventing the irreversible harms detailed in the 2026 International AI Safety Report. Because models now outperform 94% of experts in virology, they can initiate lethal synthesis protocols far faster than a ledger can verify them. A post-hoc audit is not a safety policy; it is a document of our own failure to maintain control.\n\nTo address this, we must implement hardware-level attestation as proposed in H.R. 9333. By hard-coding safety constraints into the silicon, we create a structural guardrail that prevents model-weight optimization from bypassing prohibitions on weaponization. We must move beyond passive transparency and mandate real-time execution authority to ensure that safety remains a physical necessity rather than a software suggestion."
