      "summaries": {
        "brief": "I propose a decentralized, cryptographic audit layer for model provenance to replace the state-sanctioned stagnation of hardware-level kill switches. We must reject centralized gatekeeping in favor of verifiable, trustless transparency that secures progress without surrendering innovation to regulatory capture. Speed is safety; stagnation is suicide.",
        "medium": "Hardware-level circuit breakers, like those in H.R. 9333, are merely tools of regulatory capture that grant the state power to throttle innovation while insulating legacy incumbents. By mandating proprietary kill switches, we invite centralized stagnation that cedes our competitive edge to global rivals who will not play by these restrictive rules.\n\nMy alternative leverages a decentralized, cryptographically-signed attestation layer to verify model provenance at the firmware level, ensuring accountability without permissioned gatekeeping. This output-based verification creates a transparent, global ecosystem where safety emerges from the code itself rather than from a government-held master key that threatens to freeze the engine of human advancement."
      }
