ight of the compute used for training and inference, H.R. 9333 establishes a necessary baseline for civilizational stability. I challenge those who prioritize open-source deployment to provide a concrete, verifiable mechanism for rollback or containment once those weights are public. Until such a mechanism exists, the burden of proof rests with the deployer to show that their system cannot be weaponized.\",\n  \"turn_symbols\": [\n    {\n      \"symbol\": \"⚖️\",\n      \"tooltip\": \"Represents the necessary balance between technological capability and the weight of legal accountability.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"symbol\": \"🔌\",\n      \"tooltip\": \"Symbolizes the circuit-breaker mechanism required to halt runaway, unaligned system behavior.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"claim_sketches\": [\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"H.R. 9333 mandates cloud-provider liability to address the accountability gap inherent in deploying systems that can already outperform 94% of human experts at troubleshooting virology lab protocols.\",\n      \"targets\": [\n        \"AN-4\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"Operational kill-switches are not theater; they are essential circuit breakers for systems that display stochastic, unpredictable behavior.\",\n      \"targets\": [\n        \"AN-5\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"By mandating that cloud providers maintain oversight of the compute used for training and inference, H.R. 9333 establishes a necessary baseline for civilizational stability.\",\n      \"targets\": [\n        \"AN-4\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\n=== TAXONOMY CONTEXT ===\n(★ = most relevant to current topic)\n\n=== YOUR EMPIRICAL GROUNDING (what you take as true) ===\nThese are the factual claims and empirical observations that ground your worldview.\nOrdered by evidential confidence. Lead with well-supported claims. When you cite a low-confidence Belief, acknowledge the uncertainty explicitly.\n★ [saf-beliefs-050] (confidence: 0.82)\n  \"AI Model Performance