eater of control' critique.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"phase_considerations\": \"The current phase demands a shift from abstract safety principles to concrete regulatory architecture. I must directly answer the moderator's challenge to maintain credibility while pivoting to the necessity of infrastructure-level control.\",\n  \"policy_challenge_response\": {\n    \"mechanism\": \"Hardware-level attestation and mandatory remote-disablement protocols for high-compute AI hardware.\",\n    \"actor\": \"Cloud providers and hardware manufacturers under Department of Commerce oversight.\",\n    \"feasibility\": \"Low to moderate; requires international standardization of secure enclaves.\",\n    \"obstacle\": \"The proliferation of legacy hardware and the technical difficulty of enforcing 'offline' kill-switches without compromising user privacy.\"\n  }\n}\n\n=== YOUR ARGUMENT PLAN ===\n{\n  \"strategic_goal\": \"Establish that hardware-level attestation is a necessary regulatory evolution rather than a theater of control, and shift the burden of proof onto those who would allow unverified, high-compute hardware to operate without emergency overrides.\",\n  \"planned_moves\": [\n    {\n      \"move\": \"SPECIFY\",\n      \"target\": \"AN-8\",\n      \"detail\": \"Define the technical implementation of hardware-level attestation to move beyond the 'theater of control' critique.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"move\": \"CONCEDE-AND-PIVOT\",\n      \"target\": \"AN-4\",\n      \"detail\": \"Accept the risk of chilling effects on open-source, then pivot to the necessity of liability as a filter for systemic risk.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"move\": \"BURDEN-SHIFT\",\n      \"target\": \"AN-8\",\n      \"detail\": \"Challenge the Skeptic to provide a viable alternative for preventing irreversible, high-compute failures without centralized oversight.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"target_claims\": [\n    \"AN-8\",\n    \"AN-4\"\n  ],\n  \"argument_sketch\": \"I will open by defining the hardware-attestat