" (safetyist): Maintaining meaningful human authority over AI systems: shutdown capability, veto power, goal mod...\n  regulation_precautionary → \"regulation (precautionary)\" (safetyist): Restricting AI deployment until safety has been demonstrated to a specified standard. Regulation ...\n  risk_existential → \"risk (existential)\" (safetyist): The probability of AI systems causing irreversible, humanity-ending or civilization-ending outcom...\n  risk_systemic_structural → \"risk (systemic/structural)\" (skeptic): Risk arising from concentrated power, institutional failure, and market structure rather than fro...\n  safety_alignment → \"alignment (safety)\" (safetyist): Ensuring advanced AI systems robustly pursue intended goals under distribution shift, including g...\n  safety_existential → \"safety (existential)\" (safetyist): Preventing AI systems from causing irreversible, civilization-threatening or extinction-level har...\n  safe_harbor_regulatory → \"safe harbor (regulatory)\" (safetyist): Legal protection from liability for entities that comply with specified safety standards or regul...\n  speculative_future_harm → \"harm (speculative, future)\" (safetyist): Projected catastrophic harm from future AI systems: existential risk, loss of human agency, civil...\n  speculative_risk_critique → \"risk critique (speculative vs. documented)\" (skeptic): The skeptic argument that speculative future risks (existential, catastrophic) should not overrid...\n  transparency_accountability → \"transparency (accountability)\" (safetyist): Making AI systems, their development processes, and their impacts visible to external stakeholder...\n\nDO NOT USE BARE (ambiguous across camps):\n  \"accountability\", \"alignment\", \"autonomy\", \"bias\", \"capabilities\", \"control\", \"deployment\", \"fairness\", \"frontier\", \"governance\", \"harm\", \"labor displacement\", \"oversight\", \"participatory governance\", \"performative compliance\", \"power asymmetry\", \"regulation