oncrete, verifiable rollback mechanism for when those models cause harm at scale, such as the capability to disable models that demonstrate the ability to identify 77% of software vulnerabilities as seen in 2025. The current reliance on 'decentralized resilience' is a failure to acknowledge that decentralized systems without accountability are merely unmanageable sources of systemic chaos. We spent centuries building the institutional guardrails that keep society stable; on what authority do you claim we can remove them without inviting collapse?"
