rate 76,080 synthetic hologs for 72 different wild-type proteins of concern.\n5. \"Floor Speech on Artificial Intelligence and Robotics\" — AI companies are spending $670 billion to build out data centers in 2026.\n6. \"AI Chip Supply Chain Risk 2026  Your Essential Guide\" (2026) — China established a $47.5 billion state-backed fund to accelerate its drive for semiconductor self-sufficiency.\n7. \"Sam Altman defends AIâ€™s energy toll by saying it also takes a lot to â€˜train a humanâ€™\" (2026) — Datacenters accounted for 1.5% of global electricity consumption in 2024.\n8. \"AI scale and climate commitments: A 2026 outlook\" (2026) — IT equipment, specifically chips and memory, accounts for 67% of embodied emissions in AI data centers.\n9. \"The Next Phase of AI: Technology, Infrastructure, and Policy in 2025–2026\" (2025) — Global electricity demand from data centers is projected to increase by 50 percent by 2027 and by 165 percent by 2030 compared to 2023 levels.\n10. \"Global energy demands within the AI regulatory landscape\" — Global data center electricity consumption was approximately 415 terawatt-hours in 2024, representing about 1.5% of the world's total electricity use.\n11. \"Power SeekingAIExistentialRisk\" — Advanced AI systems in simulated environments have learned to acquire and control resources (like blocks and ramps) to achieve their goals, even when not explicitly instructed to do so.\n12. \"AI, Data Centers, and the U.S. Electric Grid: A Watershed Moment\" — Dominion Energy projects nearly 27 GW of new generation by 2039, including 21 GW of renewable energy and 5.9 GW of gas.\n13. \"Situational Awareness: The Decade Ahead\" — The PRC has a hacking operation greater than every major nation combined, according to the FBI director.\n14. \"2026 Antitrust Year in Preview: AI\" (2026) — IBM closed its $6.4 billion acquisition of HashiCorp in February 2025, following an extended review by the FTC.\n15. \"AI Chip Supply Chain Risk 2026: Your Essential Guide\" (2026) — The U.S. CHIPS and Science Act has catalyzed over $630 billion in private investments to bolster the domestic semiconductor supply chain.\n\nRespond ONLY with a JSON object matching this exact schema (no markdown, no code fences):\n{\n  \"statement\": \"your full debate response (3-5 paragraphs separated by \\n\\n)\",\n  \"claim_sketches\": [\n    {\"claim\": \"near-verbatim sentence from your statement\", \"targets\": [\"AN-3\"]},\n    {\"claim\": \"near-verbatim supporting sub-claim\", \"targets\": []}\n  ],\n  \"policy_challenge_response\": {\"mechanism\": \"the specific enforcement/regulatory mechanism you propose\", \"actor\": \"who would implement and enforce it\", \"feasibility\": \"assessment of political feasibility — what coalition supports this\", \"obstacle\": \"primary implementation obstacle\"}\n}",
